Title: Generate the memory index as the top N of its directory
Created: 2026-09-10
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-10T15:50Z claude created

--- body ---

## Context

`MEMORY.md` is maintained as a list. The design makes it a **view**: regenerated
from its directory, listing the top N bodies by score, with N derived from a
character budget. That single change dissolves demotion-as-an-operation, the
orphan class, and the budget-as-a-wall — an entry below the cut is not lost, it
is simply not listed, and it returns when its score changes.

The budget already exists and already binds: `tests/test_resident_census.py`
caps each project index at 14 500 characters and the largest sits at 14 061.
The author has asked for 10 000, which cannot be applied before this ticket
ships, because today the only way under the cap is deleting index lines.

Design reference: §5 and ticket T2 in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`.

## Relevant files

- `skills/dream/SKILL.md` — where the index is currently rewritten
- `skills/dream/provenance.py` — the walker and the score inputs
- `tests/test_resident_census.py` — `BUDGETS["memory"]`, the live gate

## Actions

1. Generate the index from the directory: rank, cut at N, render.
2. Append the overflow line — how many bodies are not listed — so a reader knows
   the view is partial. The runtime's own synthesised index does this; copy the
   shape.
3. Apply it to the harness tier as well as project tiers. It is resident in
   every session and nothing in it is ever removed.
4. Score may start as recency. `0911` supplies the better inputs.

## Test

Idempotence, red first: regenerate twice, assert no diff. Then assert that a
body dropped below N is still reachable — the point of the whole design.

## Verification

- [ ] Regenerating an untouched directory produces no diff
- [ ] An index over budget is brought under it with no entry becoming
      unreachable
- [ ] The harness tier's index is generated by the same code path

## Invariants

- No body is deleted, ever, for any reason including size.
- `MEMORY.md` is never hand-edited after this lands; if it is, regeneration
  overwrites it, which is the intended behaviour and should be stated in the
  skill.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The index is generated, not authored, for both tiers
- [ ] N derives from a character budget, and the budget is a parameter
- [ ] An overflow line states how many bodies are not listed
- [ ] Regeneration is idempotent, proven by a test
